---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ReleaseCover from '../../components/ReleaseCover.astro';
import { PROJECTS } from '../../data/projects';
import { MAX_PERSON_REFERENCE, SITE_URL, WEBSITE_REFERENCE } from '../../data/site';
import telemetry from '../../data/build-telemetry.json';

const project = PROJECTS.find((item) => item.slug === 'build-telemetry')!;
const title = 'Building maccrate.ai with Hermes Agent';
const description = 'A privacy-safe field report about the decisions, detours, and release loops behind maccrate.ai.';
const canonical = `${SITE_URL}/projects/build-telemetry`;
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'TechArticle', '@id': `${canonical}#article`,
  headline: title, description, author: MAX_PERSON_REFERENCE, publisher: MAX_PERSON_REFERENCE,
  url: canonical, mainEntityOfPage: canonical, isPartOf: WEBSITE_REFERENCE, dateModified: telemetry.generatedAt,
};
const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
const compact = (n: number) => n >= 1e9 ? `${(n / 1e9).toFixed(2).replace(/0+$/, '').replace(/\.$/, '')}B` : n >= 1e6 ? `${(n / 1e6).toFixed(n >= 1e8 ? 1 : 2).replace(/\.0+$/, '')}M` : n >= 1e3 ? `${(n / 1e3).toFixed(n >= 1e5 ? 0 : 1).replace(/\.0$/, '')}K` : fmt(n);
const tokenTotal = (item: { tokens: Record<string, number> }) => Object.values(item.tokens).reduce((sum, value) => sum + value, 0);
const visibleRoute = (name: string) => name === 'Unspecified route' ? null : name;
const maxModelTokens = Math.max(...telemetry.models.map(tokenTotal));
const cartridgesProject = telemetry.projects.find((item) => item.name === 'LoRA, On Demand');
const cartridgesTokens = cartridgesProject ? Object.values(cartridgesProject.tokens).reduce((sum, value) => sum + value, 0) : 0;
const representative = telemetry.representativeSessions[0];
const traceRuns = (representative?.events || []).reduce((runs: { name: string; count: number }[], event) => {
  const name = event.toolFamily || event.skill || event.type;
  const previous = runs[runs.length - 1];
  if (previous?.name === name) previous.count += event.count || 1;
  else runs.push({ name, count: event.count || 1 });
  return runs;
}, []).filter((run) => !['SESSION START', 'MODEL REQUEST'].includes(run.name)).slice(0, 10);
---

<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} type="article" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="story" data-telemetry={JSON.stringify(telemetry)}>
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="label">HERMES AGENT FIELD REPORT · AUGUST 2026 · <a href="/about">BY MAX MACCRATE</a></p>
        <h1>The work leaves <em>a shape.</em></h1>
        <p class="intro">A private transcript can still reveal how a project gets made.</p>
        <p class="setup">{telemetry.sourceCoverage.earliestAvailable.slice(0, 10)} → {telemetry.sourceCoverage.latestIncluded.slice(0, 10)}</p>
      </div>
      <ReleaseCover project={project} />
    </header>

    <div class="body" id="article">
      <section class="lead">
        <p>MacCrate.ai is the visible result. Behind it is a record of an agentic build: model requests move through files, shell, browser, and review, with successful ideas kept and weak ones cut. In the period shown here, the retained record contains <strong>{fmt(telemetry.totals.sessions)} work sessions</strong>; {fmt(telemetry.workflow.sessionsExcluded)} heartbeat artifacts were left out. The totals below are a map of the work, not the work itself.</p>
        <dl class="totals" aria-label="Retained activity in the Hermes source record">
          <div><dt>{compact(telemetry.totals.tokens)}</dt><dd>recorded tokens<small>{compact(telemetry.totals.cacheRead)} cached context</small></dd></div>
          <div><dt>{compact(telemetry.totals.toolCalls)}</dt><dd>tool calls<small>files, shell, browser and more</small></dd></div>
          <div><dt>{fmt(telemetry.totals.sessions)}</dt><dd>work sessions<small>retained history</small></dd></div>
          <div><dt>{telemetry.totals.models}</dt><dd>models<small>{telemetry.routes.filter((item) => visibleRoute(item.name)).length} known routes</small></dd></div>
          <div><dt>{telemetry.totals.skills}</dt><dd>skills used<small>repeatable procedures</small></dd></div>
          <div><dt>{telemetry.totals.projects}</dt><dd>activity groups<small>named work plus other work</small></dd></div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The scale is large. The pattern is not random.</h2>
        <p>Different kinds of work leave different traces. Switch between tokens, sessions, and tool calls to see how the models divide the load. Model names describe inference; Codex, OpenRouter, and the local endpoint describe how those models were reached.</p>
        <div class="metric-switch" role="group" aria-label="Model chart measure">
          <button type="button" data-model-metric="tokens" aria-pressed="true">Tokens</button>
          <button type="button" data-model-metric="sessions" aria-pressed="false">Sessions</button>
          <button type="button" data-model-metric="toolCalls" aria-pressed="false">Tool calls</button>
        </div>
        <div class="model-chart exhibit" aria-label="Model participation">
          {telemetry.models.map((model) => <button type="button" class="model-row" data-model={model.name} aria-pressed="false">
            <strong>{model.name}</strong>
            <span class="bar"><i style={`width:${Math.max(2, tokenTotal(model) / maxModelTokens * 100)}%`}></i></span>
            <b data-model-value>{compact(tokenTotal(model))}</b>
            <small>{model.routes.map((item) => visibleRoute(item.name)).filter(Boolean).join(' · ') || 'route metadata unavailable'}</small>
          </button>)}
        </div>
        <p class="model-detail" aria-live="polite">Select a model for its projects and most-used tools.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>One thread: making a local model feel swappable.</h2>
        <p>The Browser Model Cartridges project makes the larger pattern tangible. The goal was not another hosted chatbot, but one local model that could take on different jobs in the browser. The work moved between runtime plumbing, adapter experiments, interface decisions, and the tests that decided which versions deserved to stay.</p>
        {cartridgesProject && <div class="project-view exhibit">
          <dl><div><dt>{cartridgesProject.sessions - cartridgesProject.childSessions}</dt><dd>main sessions</dd></div><div><dt>{cartridgesProject.childSessions}</dt><dd>child sessions</dd></div><div><dt>{fmt(cartridgesProject.toolCalls)}</dt><dd>tool calls</dd></div><div><dt>{cartridgesProject.browserSessions}</dt><dd>used the browser</dd></div></dl>
          <p>{compact(cartridgesTokens)} recorded tokens · {cartridgesProject.models.map((item) => item.name).join(' · ')} · <a href="/projects/browser-lora-cartridges">Read the project</a></p>
        </div>}
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Inside one long turn.</h2>
        <p>The words are gone, but the sequence remains. A representative cartridge session starts with skills and agent state, moves into files and shell commands, then returns to the browser for a check. Consecutive events are collapsed here so the rhythm is visible without exposing the transcript.</p>
        <div class="session-trace exhibit" aria-label="Privacy-safe session event trace">
          <p><strong>Browser Model Cartridges</strong><span>{representative?.model} · {representative?.route} · {representative?.startedAt.slice(0, 10)}</span></p>
          <ol>{traceRuns.map((run, index) => <li><b>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</b><span>{run.name}</span>{run.count > 1 && <small>× {fmt(run.count)}</small>}</li>)}</ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The build has a division of labor.</h2>
        <p>Across the full record, files, commands, and browser work dominate for a reason: an idea is not finished when a model describes it. It has to become a changed file, a running page, a tested interaction, or a release that survives review. Darker cells show more recorded calls within that model’s work.</p>
        <div class="matrix-wrap exhibit">
          <table class="matrix">
            <thead><tr><th>Model</th>{telemetry.tools.map((tool) => <th>{tool.name}</th>)}</tr></thead>
            <tbody>{telemetry.models.map((model) => {
              const row = telemetry.toolMatrix.filter((item) => item.model === model.name);
              const max = Math.max(...row.map((item) => item.count), 1);
              return <tr><th>{model.name}</th>{telemetry.tools.map((tool) => { const count = row.find((item) => item.toolFamily === tool.name)?.count || 0; return <td title={`${model.name} · ${tool.name}: ${fmt(count)}`}><i style={`opacity:${count ? .14 + (count / max) * .86 : 0}`}></i><span>{count ? compact(count) : '—'}</span></td>})}</tr>;
            })}</tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="skills-line"><strong>Most-used skills</strong>{telemetry.skills.slice(0, 5).map((skill) => <span>{skill.name} <b>{fmt(skill.count)}</b></span>)}</div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The useful part is what survives.</h2>
        <p>A count cannot explain why one idea made it into maccrate.ai and another was cut. It can show the conditions around that decision: repeated returns, delegated detours, tool work, browser checks, and the quiet accumulation of context.</p>
        <p>The discarded work is part of the project too. It gives the next attempt somewhere better to begin.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <footer class="story-end"><a href="/">← Back to projects</a></footer>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<script>
  const root = document.querySelector('[data-telemetry]');
  const data = JSON.parse(root?.dataset.telemetry || '{}');
  const format = (n) => Number(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
  const compactValue = (n) => n >= 1e9 ? `${(n / 1e9).toFixed(2).replace(/0+$/, '').replace(/\.$/, '')}B` : n >= 1e6 ? `${(n / 1e6).toFixed(n >= 1e8 ? 1 : 2).replace(/\.0+$/, '')}M` : n >= 1e3 ? `${(n / 1e3).toFixed(n >= 1e5 ? 0 : 1).replace(/\.0$/, '')}K` : format(n);
  const tokens = (item) => Object.values(item.tokens || {}).reduce((sum, value) => sum + Number(value), 0);
  let modelMetric = 'tokens';
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-model-metric]').forEach((button) => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
    modelMetric = button.dataset.modelMetric;
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-model-metric]').forEach((item) => item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', item === button ? 'true' : 'false'));
    const values = data.models.map((item) => modelMetric === 'tokens' ? tokens(item) : item[modelMetric]); const max = Math.max(...values, 1);
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-model]').forEach((row) => { const item = data.models.find((model) => model.name === row.dataset.model); const value = modelMetric === 'tokens' ? tokens(item) : item[modelMetric]; row.querySelector('.bar i').style.width = `${Math.max(2, value / max * 100)}%`; row.querySelector('[data-model-value]').textContent = compactValue(value); });
  }));
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-model]').forEach((button) => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const item = data.models.find((model) => model.name === button.dataset.model); document.querySelectorAll('[data-model]').forEach((row) => row.setAttribute('aria-pressed', row === button ? 'true' : 'false'));
    document.querySelector('.model-detail').innerHTML = `<strong>${item.name}</strong> worked across ${item.projects.map((p) => `${p.name} (${p.count})`).join(' · ')}. Most-used tools: ${item.tools.slice(0,4).map((t) => `${t.name} ${format(t.count)}`).join(' · ')}.`;
  }));
</script>

<style>
.story{--accent:#6b3fb8;max-width:1050px;margin:auto}.hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.95fr) minmax(320px,1.05fr);gap:clamp(40px,7vw,90px);align-items:center;min-height:calc(100svh - 86px);padding:20px 0;border-bottom:1px solid}.hero :global(.release-cover){width:min(100%,calc(100svh - 150px));justify-self:end}.hero-copy{min-width:0}.label,.setup{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.35;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase}.label a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:3px}.hero h1{margin:20px 0;font:400 clamp(46px,4.5vw,68px)/.96 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.045em}.hero h1 em{color:var(--accent);font-weight:400}.intro{max-width:700px;font-size:clamp(18px,1.6vw,22px);line-height:1.4}.setup{margin-top:22px}.body{max-width:790px;margin:auto}.body section{padding:64px 0;border-bottom:1px solid}.body section:last-child{padding-bottom:0;border-bottom:0}.body h2{margin:0 0 26px;font:400 clamp(34px,4vw,50px)/1.07 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em}.body p,.body li{font-size:clamp(17px,1.35vw,19px);line-height:1.7}.body p{margin:0 0 20px}.body p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}.lead>p:first-child{font-size:clamp(19px,1.7vw,23px)}.exhibit{margin:34px 0}.totals{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:28px 20px;margin:42px 0 0}.totals div{min-width:0}.totals dt{font:400 clamp(40px,5vw,62px)/1 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.055em}.totals dd{margin:8px 0 0;font-size:11px;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em}.totals small{display:block;margin-top:5px;color:#625d55;font-size:10px;font-weight:400;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0}.metric-switch{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:28px 0 14px}.metric-switch button{min-height:44px;padding:9px 13px;border:1px solid;background:transparent;cursor:pointer}.metric-switch button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#e9ff52}.model-chart{border-top:1px solid}.model-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:145px 1fr 76px;gap:14px;align-items:center;width:100%;min-height:62px;padding:12px 0;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid;background:transparent;text-align:left;cursor:pointer}.model-row[aria-pressed=true]{background:#f0ecdf}.model-row .bar{height:8px;background:#ded9ce}.model-row .bar i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--accent)}.model-row>b{font:400 21px Georgia,serif;text-align:right}.model-row small{grid-column:2/4;color:#625d55}.model-detail,.timeline-detail{min-height:28px;font-size:13px!important;color:#625d55}.timeline{margin-top:18px}.timeline-bars{display:flex;align-items:end;height:190px;gap:3px;border-bottom:1px solid}.timeline-bars button{flex:1;min-width:3px;height:100%;display:flex;align-items:end;padding:0;border:0;background:transparent;cursor:pointer}.timeline-bars i{display:block;width:100%;min-height:3px;background:var(--accent)}.timeline-bars button[aria-pressed=true] i{background:#ef4b36}.timeline-axis{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:8px;font-size:10px}.timeline-detail{margin-top:18px!important}.project-switch button{flex:1;min-width:135px;text-align:left}.project-view{padding:24px;background:#e9e3d7}.project-view :global(>div){display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:baseline}.project-view :global(>div strong){font:400 28px Georgia,serif}.project-view :global(dl){display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:18px;margin:0 0 24px}.project-view :global(dt){font:400 28px Georgia,serif}.project-view :global(dd){margin:4px 0 0;font-size:9px;text-transform:uppercase}.project-view :global(p){font-size:13px!important}.session-trace>p{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;font-size:13px!important}.session-trace ol{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;margin:16px 0 0;padding:0;list-style:none;border-top:1px solid}.session-trace li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:28px 1fr auto;gap:8px;padding:11px 12px 11px 0;border-bottom:1px solid}.session-trace li:nth-child(even){padding-left:12px;border-left:1px solid}.session-trace li b{font-size:9px;color:var(--accent)}.session-trace li span{font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.06em}.session-trace li small{font-size:10px}.matrix-wrap{overflow-x:auto}.matrix{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:10px}.matrix th,.matrix td{padding:7px;text-align:center;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.matrix thead th{writing-mode:vertical-rl;height:90px;text-align:left}.matrix thead th:first-child{writing-mode:initial;height:auto}.matrix tbody th{text-align:left;white-space:nowrap}.matrix td{position:relative;min-width:54px}.matrix td i{position:absolute;inset:4px;background:var(--accent)}.matrix td span{position:relative;z-index:1}.skills-line{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 22px;margin-top:22px;font-size:12px}.skills-line span b{color:var(--accent)}.story-end{max-width:790px;margin:32px auto 0;padding:0}.story-end a{font-size:14px;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none}:global(.site-foot){margin-top:44px}
@media(max-width:700px){.hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;min-height:0;padding:34px 0;gap:30px}.hero :global(.release-cover){order:-1;width:100%}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(44px,13vw,64px)}.body section{padding:50px 0}.body section:last-child{padding-bottom:0}.totals{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.model-row{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto}.model-row .bar{grid-column:1;grid-row:2}.model-row>b{grid-column:2;grid-row:1}.model-row small{grid-column:1/3}.timeline-bars{height:150px;gap:2px}.project-view :global(dl){grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.session-trace>p{display:block}.session-trace>p span{display:block;margin-top:6px}.session-trace ol{grid-template-columns:1fr}.session-trace li:nth-child(even){padding-left:0;border-left:0}.matrix{min-width:0}.matrix tr>*:nth-child(n+6){display:none}.matrix td{min-width:0}.story-end{margin-top:28px}}
@media(max-width:350px){.totals dt{font-size:37px}.hero h1{font-size:43px}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.story *{transition:none!important}}
</style>
